# Timing And Retry Workflow Example

This self-contained suite demonstrates a one-time pre-request wait, a configured
status retry, an expectation-aware retry, and capture from only the successful
final attempt.

## Poll An Eventually Consistent Resource

```yaml
test: eventually-ready
get: https://api.example.com/resources/current
wait_before: ${{ milliseconds(5) }}
mock_only: true
mock:
  sequence:
    - status: 404
      body:
        error: not-ready
    - status: 200
      body:
        ready: false
        resourceId: transient-attempt
    - status: 200
      body:
        ready: true
        resourceId: final-resource
expect:
  status: 200
  values:
    - key: $.ready
      op: equals
      value: true
capture:
  resource_id: $.resourceId
retry:
  attempts: 3
  delay: ${{ milliseconds(5) }}
  backoff: fixed
  statuses: [404, 409, 500, 502, 503, 504]
  expectation_failures: true
```

## Use The Final Captured Value

```yaml
test: use-final-resource
requires: eventually-ready
post: https://api.example.com/resources/use
body:
  resourceId: $resource_id
mock_only: true
mock:
  status: 204
expect:
  status: 204
```
